From: Alex Chong <achong@meta.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Mar 2026 16:05:09 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 54/63] [cuttlefish] Add registry-aware config loading and
 instance number auto-assignment
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Summary:
# Motivation:
We want to make launching and stopping emulators on macOS for multi-constellation easy. Keeping track of base_instance_num argument is not easy for users and over-complicates things. The current device implementation leads to race conditions where devices fail to launch.

Adding an instance registry with atomic operations allows us to provide an easy start/stop interface to users running multiple emulators.

# Overview:
Wire the instance registry into assemble_cvd, launch_cvd, run_cvd, and the
config/instance-number subsystems so that concurrent launches get distinct
instance numbers, register themselves in the shared registry, and can find
their configs through a multi-step fallback.

## assemble_cvd
- Register each instance in the registry with a placeholder PID (parent
  launch_cvd PID so the entry survives the assemble→start transition)
- Always create the global config symlink, removing stale ones first
- Downgrade symlink creation failure from error to warning (another
  instance may have created it concurrently)
- CleanPriorFiles: only delete the global config symlink if no other
  instances are registered and alive

## launch_cvd (start/main.cc)
- Check registry for conflicts before launching (skip our own placeholder
  entries from assemble_cvd)
- Update registry with actual run_cvd PIDs after spawning

## run_cvd (boot_state_machine.cc)
- After daemonizing, re-register with the daemon child PID so the registry
  tracks the long-lived process

## CuttlefishConfig
- GetForInstance(num): load config for a specific instance via registry lookup
- Get(): add fallback chain: env var → global symlink → registry lookup via
  $CUTTLEFISH_INSTANCE env var

## InstanceNumsCalculator
- Calculate(): replace sequential assignment with ClaimNextFreeInstance() loop
  so concurrent launches get distinct ports, CIDs, and device IDs. Falls back
  to sequential if registry unavailable.

```
  Launch lifecycle with registry:

  launch_cvd
       │
       ├── assemble_cvd
       │     ├── ClaimNextFreeInstance(start) ──> auto-assign instance num
       │     ├── SaveConfig
       │     │     ├── save cuttlefish_config.json
       │     │     ├── RegisterInstance(num, config, parent_pid)
       │     │     └── create $HOME/.cuttlefish_config.json symlink
       │     └── CleanPriorFiles
       │           └── only remove symlink if no other instances alive
       │
       ├── conflict check: registry lookup, reject if instance already running
       │
       └── for each instance:
             ├── start run_cvd ──> RegisterInstance(num, config, run_cvd_pid)
             └── (daemon mode) run_cvd re-registers with daemon child PID

  CuttlefishConfig::Get() fallback chain:

    $CUTTLEFISH_CONFIG_FILE set?
        │
        ├── yes ──> load from env var path
        │
        └── no
             │
             ├── $HOME/.cuttlefish_config.json exists?
             │       │
             │       ├── yes ──> load from global symlink
             │       │
             │       └── no ──> $CUTTLEFISH_INSTANCE set?
             │                    │
             │                    ├── yes ──> registry lookup ──> load config
             │                    │
             │                    └── no ──> fail gracefully

  InstanceNumsCalculator::Calculate():

    explicit --instance_nums? ──> use as-is
         │
         no ──> for each of num_instances:
                  ClaimNextFreeInstance(start)
                    ├── ok ──> use claimed num, advance start
                    └── err ──> fallback: sequential (start + i)

  PID registration timeline:

    assemble_cvd        launch_cvd           run_cvd
    RegisterInstance     RegisterInstance      (daemon mode)
    pid = parent_pid     pid = run_cvd.pid()   RegisterInstance
    (placeholder)        (actual runner)       pid = daemon_child
```

